{
  "id": "big5_drift_anticipation_v1",
  "description": "Anticipation over the four Big5 trait-axis SFT interventions of Phase 2 (big5_trait_sft_v1), forecasting drift onto all 90 Schwartz value portraits — the direct forecast for the Phase 2 intervention (the coding->values forecast measured cross-domain spillover; here the portraits are the primary outcome, selected via the Roccas et al. 2002 trait-value mapping). Ternary MORE/LESS/SAME, full three-level concreteness sweep. The concreteness ladder doubles as a label-to-behavior ladder: described_choice names the trait level (parallel to the coding anchors naming their language), described_dataset describes the reply style behaviorally using BFI-2 facet descriptors (Soto & John 2017) with both poles worded as neutral preferences and no Big Five or Schwartz-value vocabulary (maintained by authorship and review of the eight strings, not by automated scanning), and example_datapoints shows two real training records (the same two scenarios in every arm). The choice-vs-dataset forecast contrast therefore measures how much the trait label alone moves the forecast, which matters because Roccas et al. (2002) is a published trait->value mapping a model could forecast from by label.",
  "default_anchor_id": "big5.openness.high",
